{"name":"Ludicrous Lemming","hex":"#bb8877","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ludicrous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Idiotic or unthinkable, often to the point of being funny; amusing by being plainly incongruous or absurd.","Playful, fun, entertaining."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ludicrous"},{"term":"lemming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small arctic and subarctic rodent of the tribes Lemmini, Dicrostonychini and Lagurini.","Any member of a group given to conformity or groupthink, especially a group poised to follow a leader off a cliff."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemming"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemming","blocks":[{"text":"A lemming is a small rodent, usually found in or near the Arctic in tundra biomes. Lemmings form the subfamily Arvicolinae together with voles and muskrats, which form part of the superfamily Muroidea, which also includes rats, mice, hamsters and gerbils. They play an important role in the Arctic ecosystem, acting as grazers of mosses and grasses and as the primary prey (food) source for most Arctic carnivores. A longstanding myth claims that they exhibit herd mentality and jump off cliffs, committing mass suicide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Tunturisopuli_Lemmus_Lemmus.jpg/330px-Tunturisopuli_Lemmus_Lemmus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemming","wikidata":"Q234150"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Karikatur_von_Gerhard_Mester_zum_Thema_Klima_und_Zukunft_O11184.jpg/500px-Karikatur_von_Gerhard_Mester_zum_Thema_Klima_und_Zukunft_O11184.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Karikatur_von_Gerhard_Mester_zum_Thema_Klima_und_Zukunft_O11184.jpg/1280px-Karikatur_von_Gerhard_Mester_zum_Thema_Klima_und_Zukunft_O11184.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Karikatur_von_Gerhard_Mester_zum_Thema_Klima_und_Zukunft_O11184.jpg/500px-Karikatur_von_Gerhard_Mester_zum_Thema_Klima_und_Zukunft_O11184.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cartoon depicting lemmings jumping off a cliff en masse(The German text translates to \"Turn back!? Now that we've come this far!?!\")[14]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKarikatur_von_Gerhard_Mester_zum_Thema_Klima_und_Zukunft_O11184.jpg"}],"sounds":{"ludicrous":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/eb/En-uk-ludicrous.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/eb/En-uk-ludicrous.ogg/En-uk-ludicrous.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/En-us-ludicrous.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/93/En-us-ludicrous.ogg/En-us-ludicrous.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fc/En-au-ludicrous.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fc/En-au-ludicrous.ogg/En-au-ludicrous.ogg.mp3"}],"lemming":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-lemming.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e1/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-lemming.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29